The source trail is:
 Makemon.c#line890, Makemon.c#line1203, Questpgr.c#qt_montype,
You.h#line76, Role.c#line1388, Role.c#line94.

So yes, in the caveman quest dungeon branch, 3% of all random spawns
are replaced with non-extinctable H, which means titans in your case.

By "only bugbears were defined" you likely mean the ad-hoc rule
rndmonst() will only make monsters whose difficulty is less than the
average of your and the dungeon's level. Rndmonst() is responsible for
the vast majority of monsters generated, but not all of them. In this
case, mkclass() is the culprit, and it handles tough monsters
differently: they become exponentially unlikely. Not much of a
consulation if only titans are left to chose from.


